# Copy this file to .env (which is gitignored — never commit your real key) and fill in
# GEMINI_API_KEY (or OPENAI_API_KEY) to use scripts/content-generate.ts. Get a free-tier Gemini
# key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — see docs/content-generation.md for setup and usage.

# Which provider scripts/content-generate.ts calls: gemini (default) or openai.
# `--provider <gemini|openai>` on the command line wins over this.
# AI_PROVIDER=gemini

GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Model to use (default: gemini-3.8-flash, the DEFAULT_MODEL constant in
# scripts/content-generate.ts; `--model <name>` on the command line wins over this).
# MODEL NAMES CHANGE and old ones are retired: if a run fails with 404 / "model not found",
# look up a current name in AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com) or at
# https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models and set it here.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# Optional: thinking level for Gemini 3 models (low | high). Unset = the model's default.
# Higher = slower and uses more of the free quota, usually better drafts. Override per run with --thinking.
# GEMINI_THINKING_LEVEL=high

# ---- OpenAI (only needed when AI_PROVIDER=openai / --provider openai) ----

# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# REQUIRED when using the openai provider — there is no hardcoded default model (OpenAI retires
# and renames model ids). Check a current "mini"-class model (cheap, fast) on
# https://platform.openai.com/docs/pricing and set its id here, or pass --model <name>.
# OPENAI_MODEL=

# Optional: reasoning effort for reasoning-capable models (low | medium | high). Unset = the
# model's default. Sent as `reasoning_effort`; override per run with --thinking.
# OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=medium

# Optional: overrides MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS (65536) for `max_completion_tokens` — some OpenAI models
# cap lower than that.
# OPENAI_MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS=32768
